{
  "sn19.1:0.1": "Linked Discourses 19.1 ",
  "sn19.1:0.2": "Chapter One ",
  "sn19.1:0.3": "A Skeleton ",
  "sn19.1:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn19.1:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "sn19.1:1.3": "Now at that time Venerable Mark and Venerable Mahāmoggallāna were staying on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. ",
  "sn19.1:1.4": "Then Mahāmoggallāna robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to Mark and said to him, ",
  "sn19.1:1.5": "“Come, Reverend Mark, let’s enter Rājagaha for alms.” ",
  "sn19.1:1.6": "“Yes, reverend,” Mark replied. ",
  "sn19.1:1.7": "As Mahāmoggallāna was descending from Vulture’s Peak Mountain he smiled at a certain spot. ",
  "sn19.1:1.8": "So Mark said to Mahāmoggallāna, ",
  "sn19.1:1.9": "“What is the cause, Reverend Moggallāna, what is the reason you smiled?” ",
  "sn19.1:1.10": "“Reverend Mark, it’s the wrong time for this question. ",
  "sn19.1:1.11": "Ask me when we’re in the Buddha’s presence.” ",
  "sn19.1:2.1": "Then Mark and Mahāmoggallāna wandered for alms in Rājagaha. After the meal, on their return from almsround, they went to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. Mark said to Mahāmoggallāna: ",
  "sn19.1:2.2": "“Just now, as Mahāmoggallāna was descending from Vulture’s Peak Mountain he smiled at a certain spot. ",
  "sn19.1:2.3": "What is the cause, Reverend Moggallāna, what is the reason you smiled?” ",
  "sn19.1:3.